BT /F1 11 Tf 50 700 Td (Photosynthesis is how green plants and some other organisms make their own food using sunlight. Plants absorb carbon dioxide from the air and water from the ground. The chlorophyll inside chloroplasts captures light energy, which powers a reaction that produces glucose and oxygen. The simplified equation is six CO2 plus six H2O plus light energy gives C6H12O6 plus six O2. Photosynthesis is critical to life on Earth because it generates atmospheric oxygen and underpins almost every food chain.) Tj ET
